  "id": "03-backdated-inward-revalues-outward",
  "description": "WHY STOCK VALUE IS NEVER STORED. PUR-1 is entered on 20-Apr but DATED 05-Apr, i.e. before an issue that has already been valued. Replay order is by voucher_date, so PUR-1 (10 @ 100.0000 = 1000.0000) lands first, then PUR-2 dated 10-Apr (10 @ 200.0000 = 2000.0000) -> 20.0000 units / 3000.0000 @ 150.0000, and SAL-1 dated 15-Apr consumes 5*150.0000 = 750.0000, closing 15.0000 / 2250.0000 @ 150.0000. WITHOUT the back-dated PUR-1 the very same SAL-1 consumed 5*200.0000 = 1000.0000 and the closing was 5.0000 / 1000.0000 @ 200.0000. One already-posted, unedited outward changed its cost by 250.0000 because an OLDER voucher appeared: a materialised value could not have expressed that, which is the whole architecture. Note PUR-1's versionCreatedAt is the LATEST of the three - entry order must not affect the answer.",
